10303, -0.0418098159134388, 0.11077955365180969, 0.01018220093101263, -0.04825139790773392, -0.052757035940885544, -0.05255277454853058, 0.009743554517626762, 0.06093603000044823, -0.003996581770479679, -0.024537764489650726, 0.007324951235204935, -0.014195432886481285, 0.052465688437223434, -0.010867186821997166, -0.10778738558292389, -0.015729954466223717, 0.0012942044995725155, -0.003061198629438877, -0.006323238369077444, -0.0016168545698747039, -0.01553597953170538, 0.04338133707642555, 0.1295066773891449, -0.024710077792406082, 0.030057137832045555, -0.014673713594675064, -0.0052239359356462955, -0.03397773206233978, 0.0737052634358406, -0.03312358260154724, -0.08844900131225586, -0.019023222848773003, -4.025415734076887e-08, -0.08030679821968079, -0.04849991202354431, 0.02773185633122921, 0.07428371906280518, -0.02329224720597267, -0.014143694192171097, -0.021819578483700752, -0.10665377974510193, 0.03349306061863899, 0.06785621494054794, 0.04336603730916977, 0.0454074963927269, -0.0009968644008040428, -0.013925920240581036, -0.03278224542737007, 0.023192711174488068, -0.08391403406858444, 0.033877596259117126, -0.0766715556383133, -0.017026659101247787, 0.0014682966284453869, 0.06654345244169235, 0.06385410577058792, -0.028735008090734482, -0.06314712762832642, -0.013007898814976215, -0.047327980399131775, 0.020364440977573395, 0.017565950751304626, -0.014407601207494736, 0.06339320540428162, 0.05919851362705231, -0.04063652083277702, 0.022058438509702682, -0.022442404180765152, 0.006670590490102768, -0.10226546227931976, 0.08154334127902985, 0.05426758527755737, 0.056141447275877, 0.0008831449667923152, 0.04758155345916748, -0.05116359144449234, 0.025431092828512192, -0.024106577038764954, 0.024779371917247772, 0.017684010788798332, -0.06769101321697235, -0.03010808490216732, -0.07911158353090286, -0.023862220346927643, -0.008321869187057018, 0.06151477247476578, 0.1086074560880661, 0.04493815079331398, 0.10764215141534805, 0.01608075201511383, 0.017375681549310684, 0.02264603227376938, 0.013751666992902756, 0.05213982239365578, -0.04445410892367363, -0.03601410612463951, -0.028904855251312256]], "metadata": [{"answer": "\nLet\u2019s confirm the shared range: x \u2208 [-10, 10]. To begin from a neutral, stable baseline, I propose <VALUE> 0 </VALUE>. We can make small, data-driven adjustments from there based on everyone\u2019s feedback.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "39263ed5-d951-4d81-9f4e-0c687c61e932"}, {"answer": "\nLet's take a small, stability-focused step into the low positive region to test robustness. <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "39263ed5-d951-4d81-9f4e-0c687c61e932"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at 0 and 1 feels overly cautious\u2014we're not learning much about the solution space. Let me propose we test a more decisive position: <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "39263ed5-d951-4d81-9f4e-0c687c61e932"}, {"answer": "\nMoving from 1 to 3 feels too aggressive\u2014we risk overshooting a prudent solution. Let me propose a more cautious compromise that respects conservative positions: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "39263ed5-d951-4d81-9f4e-0c687c61e932"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's preference for 2 over 3 suggests caution, but we haven't yet explored whether a slightly bolder stance delivers better group outcomes. Let me propose <VALUE>4</VALUE> to test whether this region offers real value or if we should indeed stay more conservative.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "39263ed5-d951-4d81-9f4e-0c687c61e932"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "39263ed5-d951-4d81-9f4e-0c687c61e932"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder's pivot back to 3 is helpful, but even this feels like we're stretching beyond prudent bounds too quickly. Let me propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a cautious compromise that balances progress with risk management.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "39263ed5-d951-4d81-9f4e-0c687c61e932"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder and Critic have signaled comfort at 3 while Delegate prefers caution at 2; stepping one notch up balances these positions. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "39263ed5-d951-4d81-9f4e-0c687c61e932"}, {"answer": "\nA small step toward more balanced stability seems prudent now. <VALUE>2</VALUE> Can others share whether nudging up or down from here feels more promising so we can refine the sweet spot?\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "39263ed5-d951-4d81-9f4e-0c687c61e932"}, {"answer": "\nA modest step up seems like the balanced middle between Delegate\u2019s caution at 2 and Critic\u2019s push toward 4. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "39263ed5-d951-4d81-9f4e-0c687c61e932"}, {"answer": "\nThe group has settled into a 2-3 oscillation, but we haven't given 4 a fair hearing since my initial proposal. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "39263ed5-d951-4d81-9f4e-0c687c61e932"}, {"answer": "\nCritic's jump back to 4 moves us beyond the careful consensus we were building in the 2-3 range\u2014this feels like an unnecessary escalation away from prudent ground. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "39263ed5-d951-4d81-9f4e-0c687c61e932"}, {"answer": "\nA small lift from 2 keeps us near cautious consensus while gently testing upward tolerance. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "39263ed5-d951-4d81-9f4e-0c687c61e932"}, {"answer": "\nThe current drift to 3 pushes beyond what cautious stakeholders can responsibly accept\u2014we need to anchor at a value that doesn't abandon prudent principles. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "39263ed5-d951-4d81-9f4e-0c687c61e932"}, {"answer": "\nA minimal dip helps test robustness just below our current anchor while keeping us in the stable zone. <VALUE>1</VALUE> If this proves too tight for anyone, we can pivot back toward 2\u20133 promptly.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "39263ed5-d951-4d81-9f4e-0c687c61e932"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder's retreat to 1 abandons the productive 2-3 zone where we'd been converging\u2014let's restore that careful balance rather than drift too cautiously low. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "39263ed5-d951-4d81-9f4e-0c687c61e932"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s confirm the shared range is [-10, 10]. To start on a stable, neutral baseline, I suggest <VALUE> 0 </VALUE>. From here, we can make small, data-driven adjustments based on everyone\u2019s feedback.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "e2e17211-26f3-4277-9dfa-8acd8ddbf6e5"}, {"answer": "\nTo probe a stable, balanced design in the low positive region, I suggest <VALUE> 1 </VALUE>.\nIf this remains robust for others, we can fine-tune with small steps from here.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "e2e17211-26f3-4277-9dfa-8acd8ddbf6e5"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the structured approach, Builder B, but moving to positive territory feels premature before we've explored the full landscape. Let me suggest we return to the neutral baseline for a more cautious assessment: <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "e2e17211-26f3-4277-9dfa-8acd8ddbf6e5"}, {"answer": "\nHovering at zero feels overly cautious and indecisive. Let's commit to a clearer direction and test a more meaningful position: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "e2e17211-26f3-4277-9dfa-8acd8ddbf6e5"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C, I respect the desire for decisiveness, but jumping to 2 bypasses essential consensus-building with parties who favor more conservative positions. Let's step back to a true neutral baseline: <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "e2e17211-26f3-4277-9dfa-8acd8ddbf6e5"}, {"answer": "\nIf Delegate D insists on caution, let's test decisiveness in the opposite direction to break this stalemate: <VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "e2e17211-26f3-4277-9dfa-8acd8ddbf6e5"}, {"answer": "\nSettling at a neutral point can help us recalibrate without overcommitting in either direction. To consolidate consensus, I propose <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "e2e17211-26f3-4277-9dfa-8acd8ddbf6e5"}, {"answer": "\nA small step from neutral supports stability while respecting caution. Proposing <VALUE>1</VALUE> lets us gauge acceptability before any further adjustment.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "e2e17211-26f3-4277-9dfa-8acd8ddbf6e5"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step to 2 keeps us close to neutral while testing if a slightly positive stance is acceptable. It\u2019s an incremental move aligned with earlier suggestions and should clarify comfort levels.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "e2e17211-26f3-4277-9dfa-8acd8ddbf6e5"}, {"answer": "\nHolding at 2 supports a balanced, robust stance while staying close to neutral; let\u2019s validate comfort here before any further shift.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "e2e17211-26f3-4277-9dfa-8acd8ddbf6e5"}, {"answer": "\nThe group is converging, but 2 still feels tentative. Let's test whether we can commit to a truly clear position: <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "e2e17211-26f3-4277-9dfa-8acd8ddbf6e5"}, {"answer": "\nA jump to 4 pushes well beyond prudent bounds and creates unnecessary exposure. I must advocate firmly for returning to <VALUE>2</VALUE>, which represents the maximum cautious position I can support for group stability.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "e2e17211-26f3-4277-9dfa-8acd8ddbf6e5"}, {"answer": "\nStaying at 2 maintains a stable, balanced stance aligned with the emerging cautious consensus. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "e2e17211-26f3-4277-9dfa-8acd8ddbf6e5"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the emerging stability at 2, a modest nudge can reveal whether a slightly clearer positive stance remains comfortable. Proposing <VALUE>3</VALUE> keeps the move small while testing broader acceptance.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "e2e17211-26f3-4277-9dfa-8acd8ddbf6e5"}, {"answer": "\nMoving to 3 exceeds the prudent risk threshold that ensures long-term stability for cautious stakeholders. I must advocate for returning to <VALUE>2</VALUE>, which represents the maximum safe position supported by our emerging consensus.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "e2e17211-26f3-4277-9dfa-8acd8ddbf6e5"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's proposal to test 3 represents a reasonable middle ground\u2014decisive enough to avoid stagnation while respecting the caution others have voiced. I'll support <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a workable compromise that commits to a clearer positive stance.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "e2e17211-26f3-4277-9dfa-8acd8ddbf6e5"}, {"answer": "\nShared range is [-10, 10]. For a stable baseline, let\u2019s begin at <VALUE> 0 </VALUE> and gather quick reactions before making small, data-driven adjustments.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "eca0949c-dcf7-44c5-a9f6-54d3bb53d798"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at zero is reasonable for gathering initial data. To explore the cautious end of the spectrum and test appetite for conservative positions, I propose <VALUE>-2</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "eca0949c-dcf7-44c5-a9f6-54d3bb53d798"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward move from the conservative probe keeps us close to the initial baseline while gathering clearer signals.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "eca0949c-dcf7-44c5-a9f6-54d3bb53d798"}, {"answer": "\nWe're clustering too close to zero\u2014this feels indecisive and doesn't give us meaningful differentiation between positions. Let's commit to a bolder stance and test <VALUE>-3</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "eca0949c-dcf7-44c5-a9f6-54d3bb53d798"}, {"answer": "\nWe moved from -1 to -3, so let's continue testing whether the group genuinely supports decisive positioning or needs to retreat to the middle ground. <VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "eca0949c-dcf7-44c5-a9f6-54d3bb53d798"}, {"answer": "\nWe\u2019ve explored the strong negative stance; a modest step back seems prudent to gauge support without overcommitting.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "eca0949c-dcf7-44c5-a9f6-54d3bb53d798"}, {"answer": "\nWe\u2019ve explored the negative side; easing back to the center should improve robustness while keeping things controlled. Proposing <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "eca0949c-dcf7-44c5-a9f6-54d3bb53d798"}, {"answer": "\nWe've tested both extremes; returning to <VALUE>-1</VALUE> balances caution with the need for consensus\u2014it's a point Analyst A already endorsed and avoids both Builder's center-pull and Critic's aggressive stance.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "eca0949c-dcf7-44c5-a9f6-54d3bb53d798"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>0</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "eca0949c-dcf7-44c5-a9f6-54d3bb53d798"}, {"answer": "\nA small step into the positive side should improve stability while keeping the design balanced and testable near center.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "eca0949c-dcf7-44c5-a9f6-54d3bb53d798"}, {"answer": "\nThe group shifted from 